# score: Mambo del Telar (hilo puro)
# summary: the mambo played by one instrument — plucked-body percussion, breath shakers, a stiff-string cencerro, glossy midpoint bells for brass, and the band's own strings underneath
# tempo: 182
# time: 4/4
# key: Cm
# bars: 76
# reverb: 1.0
# master: rms=-14

# text @b1: no samples, no oscillators. every voice below is the string
# text @b1: network: the claves are mandolin-bodied clicks, the congas are
# text @b1: cello-bodied thumps, the guiro is the hilo breathing, the
# text @b1: cencerro is a stiff string struck at its midpoint.
# text @b25: the brass section is bells now — midpoint plucks, even
# text @b25: harmonics gone, dispersion for the sheen. glossy and round.
# text @b35: somewhere above, a braid is being tied. listen for the plucks
# text @b35: whose rings re-voice themselves.

# instruments:
#   cl = claves (perc, synth=pluck, bodyp=mandolin, sus=0.15, damp=0.6, pick=0.95, pos=0.08, body=0.5, gain=-8, send=0.08)
#   cb = cencerro (perc, synth=weave, bodyp=mandolin, stiff=0.7, pos=0.5, sus=0.6, damp=0.45, pick=0.9, courses=5, dimension=1.3, couple=0.04, body=0.4, gain=-10, send=0.1)
#   cg = congas (perc, synth=pluck, bodyp=cello, sus=0.3, damp=0.5, pos=0.45, pick=0.5, body=1.0, body_size=1.15, gain=-2, send=0.08)
